WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:21.120
Two synthetic runbooks cover the same VPN error on different product versions.

2
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:45.440
Ask the assistant about the fictional company's VPN ticket.

3
00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:53.640
The assistant selects the ticket's version-specific runbook and cites its source.

4
00:00:53.640 --> 00:01:19.680
Ask to add the sourced steps as a suggested work note.

5
00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.720
Open the demo ticket to review its suggested fix.

6
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:31.980
Open the note to review the sourced steps and their suggested status.

7
00:01:31.980 --> 00:02:16.300
Ask about the same VPN error on the other product version.

8
00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:22.720
The assistant selects that version's runbook and cites its source.

9
00:02:22.720 --> 00:03:07.800
Ask about a synthetic ticket that needs another runbook.

10
00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:14.720
The uncovered ticket becomes a counted follow-up for the knowledge team.

11
00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:22.920
Open the knowledge-team board to review the follow-up record.
